          <mxGeometry x="12" y="391.0" width="36" height="18" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s_prv_t" value="Private subnets: route to the one NAT gateway" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="leg">
          <mxGeometry x="58" y="384" width="214" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s_int" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;fillColor=#EEF0F3;strokeColor=#7D8998;" vertex="1" parent="leg">
          <mxGeometry x="12" y="424.0" width="36" height="18" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s_int_t" value="Internal subnets: local routes only" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="leg">
          <mxGeometry x="58" y="422" width="214" height="22" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s_stack" value="system/ecr" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=9;fontColor=#687078;" vertex="1" parent="leg">
          <mxGeometry x="12" y="482.0" width="46" height="16" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s_stack_t" value="Small grey text: the Terraform stack. system/ paths are under terraform/; global/ and prod01-us-east-1/ paths under terraform/environments/innovate-inc/; cluster/ and app-services/ paths under its prod01-us-east-1/" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="leg">
          <mxGeometry x="58" y="450" width="214" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="steps" value="&lt;table style=&quot;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;color:#232F3E;line-height:1.35;&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot; style=&quot;padding:2px 5px 6px 5px;font-weight:bold;font-size:15px;&quot;&gt;Step: what happens&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DNS answer, every path.&lt;/b&gt; The browser asks Route 53. The public zone answers with an A alias: web. and the apex to CloudFront; app., api. and load. to the accelerator's static IPv4 addresses; argocd. to the Ingress ALB.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot; style=&quot;padding:8px 5px 3px 5px;font-weight:bold;font-size:12px;color:#232F3E;&quot;&gt;Path A, the single-page app (web. and the apex)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;A2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TLS termination.&lt;/b&gt; At the nearest CloudFront edge, with the ACM certificate for web. and the apex (TLSv1.2_2021, SNI only). Plain HTTP gets a redirect to HTTPS.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;A3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WAF check.&lt;/b&gt; The CLOUDFRONT web ACL runs the IP reputation list, the Common Rule Set and Known Bad Inputs. More than 2000 requests from one IP in 300 s get 429.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;A4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Routing decision.&lt;/b&gt; The viewer-request function sends the apex to web. with a 301. The one cache behavior (Managed-CachingOptimized) answers a cached object at the edge.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;A5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Target selection.&lt;/b&gt; On a cache miss, Lambda@Edge adds the origin secret as User-Agent and CloudFront fetches the object over HTTP from the bucket's website endpoint; the bucket policy checks the secret. 403 and 404 become /index.html with 200, so app routes load.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;A6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Response.&lt;/b&gt; Lambda@Edge adds HSTS, nosniff, Referrer-Policy and CORS headers for web.; CloudFront caches and returns the object.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot; style=&quot;padding:8px 5px 3px 5px;font-weight:bold;font-size:12px;color:#232F3E;&quot;&gt;Path B, the API through the accelerator (app., api., load.)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;B2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Accelerator.&lt;/b&gt; The request enters the AWS network at the nearest edge location on the TCP 80 or 443 listener and goes to the nearest healthy endpoint group, us-east-1 or us-west-2 (traffic dial 100 each, TCP 443 health check). The endpoint is that region's public ALB; the client IP is kept.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;B3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TLS termination.&lt;/b&gt; On the public ALB's HTTPS listener (ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06) with the ACM certificate for app., api. or load.; port 80 answers with a 301 to 443.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;B4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WAF check.&lt;/b&gt; The regional web ACL runs IP reputation, the Common Rule Set, the blacklisted-ips set, SQLi and Known Bad Inputs, then limits each IP to 2000 requests per 300 s. A blocked request gets 403.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;B5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Routing decision.&lt;/b&gt; Host rules: priority 10 sends api. and priority 20 sends load. to their target groups, priority 100 sends app. to prod01-us-edge-ingress; any other host gets the fixed 403.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;B6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Target selection.&lt;/b&gt; The groups take pod IPs on port 8000. TargetGroupBindings register of-api's pods on x86 nodes and of-load's on Graviton nodes. Nothing registers targets in prod01-us-edge-ingress on the rollout, so app. gets 503 here.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan=&quot;2&quot; style=&quot;padding:8px 5px 3px 5px;font-weight:bold;font-size:12px;color:#232F3E;&quot;&gt;Path C, the Ingress ALB (argocd. in us-east-1, argocd-usw2. in us-west-2)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;C2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TLS termination.&lt;/b&gt; On the Ingress ALB's HTTPS 443 listener with the argocd. certificate. This ALB has no WAF check.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;C3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Routing decision.&lt;/b&gt; Host argocd. goes to the argocd-server Service; any other host gets the controller's fixed 404.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;width:30px;font-weight:bold;color:#1E8900;&quot;&gt;C4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;vertical-align:top;padding:3px 5px;border-top:1px solid #D5DBDB;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Target selection.&lt;/b&gt; The controller registers the argocd-server pod IPs directly (target type ip). Argo CD has no node selector.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#AAB7B8;rounded=1;arcSize=1;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1012" width="870" height="700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
